  {% if isBeta %}
    <details class='beta-faq'>
      <summary>FAQs for pk-gov-beta</summary>
      <details>
        <summary>What does 'beta' mean?</summary>
        <p>
          pk-gov-beta is like an 'early bird' version of the existing pk-gov you know and love. This
          means new features, services and other experiements being developed by the Ministry of
          Technology are tested here first, before being pushed onto pk-gov. Note that this mean
          pk-gov-beta is less stable than pk-gov, so bugs may be present.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is all pk-gov functionality available?</summary>
        <p>
          Yes...maybe. Parts of pk-gov that are not being worked on will retain identical
          functionality, while parts that are in active development can vary in functionality, from
          being unchanged to having new behaviour.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Can I continue to use pk-gov services?</summary>
        <p>
          All pk-gov services are operational here, though as mentioned in the question above, some
          functionality may be different from the existing pk-gov service. If drastic changes have
          been made or a service is temporarily unusable, updates will be provided in the Government
          news page.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>Is this really what the Ministry of Technology uses internally?</summary>
        <p>
          Not exactly, but its much closer than the 'stable' pk-gov. Typically, new feature
          development begins in private branches not exposed to the public. Once the new feature is
          in a usable state, it will be added to pk-gov-beta, and finally released on pk-gov once
          development is fully complete!
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>I can't find any differences compared to the 'stable' site.</summary>
        <p>
          The development of pk-gov tends to happen in bursts, which is why our updates often
          deliver several features at once. As a result, there can be periods of inactivity where no
          new features are added to pk-gov-beta.
        </p>
      </details>
      <details>
        <summary>How can I report an issue or send feedback?</summary>
        <p>
          If you encounter a bug, are unable to use pk-gov-beta properly or want to give feedback,
          you can use the 'Report an issue' or 'Send feedback' buttons above the footer (This opens
          an Issue in pk-gov's GitHub repository).
        </p>
      </details>
    </details>
  {% endif %}
